I'll write a reusable pattern:

```java
private static final class CaptureHandler extends java.util.logging.Handler {
    private final java.util.List<java.util.logging.LogRecord> records = java.util.Collections.synchronizedList(new java.util.ArrayList<>());
    private final String idFragment;
    private final CountDownLatch count = new CountDownLatch(1);
    private volatile boolean throwing;
    private volatile CountDownLatch block;
    CaptureHandler(String idFragment) { this.idFragment = idFragment; }
    @Override public void publish(java.util.logging.LogRecord record) {
        if (record.getMessage() != null && record.getMessage().contains(idFragment)) {
            records.add(record);
            count.countDown();
        }
    }
    @Override public void flush() {}
    @Override public void close() {}
}
```

